    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "solution": "Step 1: The incircle lies entirely within the interior of the triangle.\nStep 2: The centre of the incircle (incentre) must always lie inside the boundaries of the triangle.\nStep 3: Hence, the incentre is always in the interior of the triangle.",
